class_name MapData
## The named maps (built by MapGen._named). Each is turned through its middle (180 degrees):
## everything listed is drawn where it's listed and again on the other side, so every
## player has a twin spot with the same ground. A river that runs through the middle is
## listed whole, along a line that is its own twin.
##
##   name, size [W, H], mode ("1v1" ... "4v4"), biome ("a" or "a+b", mixed by "mix":
##   "patch" | "middle" | "diag"), seed (its own dice: the map always looks the same),
##   about (the lobby's line)
##   bases: side A's players, in order (side B's twins come in the same order):
##     hall [x, y] (top-left cell of the 5 x 4 hall spot), hill [cx, cy, rx, ry] (the main's
##     plateau), ramp [x, y] (its one ramp faces this point), nat [x, y] (its natural)
##   thirds: more hall spots on side A (their twins are added)
##   pieces: ["hill", cx, cy, rx, ry, [[ramp toward], ...]], ["mesa", cx, cy, rx, ry],
##     ["ridge", [[x, y], ...], width] (a cliff wall), ["lake", cx, cy, rx, ry],
##     ["river", [[x, y], ...], width, [ford at 0..1 along it, ...], ford length],
##     ["forest" | "rocks", cx, cy, rx, ry, density], ["treeline", [[x, y], ...], width,
##     [gap at 0..1, ...], gap length, "tree" | "rock"], ["clear", cx, cy, r]
##   woods: random tree / rock clumps; sites: [x, y, kit] decoration groups (MapGen.KITS);
##   decor: how much small decoration (1 = normal); water / ford: the tiles for all its water
##   and fords (when two biomes would draw them differently).

